# AGENTS.md

**Read `CLAUDE.md` in this directory — it is the whole contract, and this file has no content of
its own.**

This file exists as a copy rather than a symlink because `magik new` could not create one on the
platform that generated this app (Windows without Developer Mode is the usual reason). That is a
degraded mode: two files can drift, one file cannot. If your platform supports symlinks, replace it:

```bash
rm AGENTS.md && ln -s CLAUDE.md AGENTS.md
```
